    title: "Report: Netanyahu's allies open to unity government without Ben Gvir’s party",
    summary: "Report: Netanyahu's allies open to unity government without Ben Gvir’s party Associates of Benjamin Netanyahu have told Yashar party leader Gadi Eisenkot’s team they would accept a unity government without National Security Minister Itamar Ben Gvir's party, according to the daily Israel Hayom. Netanyahu’s associates said that Likud could let go of Otzma Yehudit (Jewish Power) if negotiations opened on a broad coalition. Speaking to figures in Eisenkot’s bloc, they also indicated US demands for Ben Gvir's Otzma Yehudit's exclusion. would not insist on including Otzma Yehudit (Jewish Power) if negotiations opened on a broad coalition. They also told figures in Eisenkot’s bloc that Washington was demanding Otzma Yehudit's exclusion. However, Likud has denied conveying such messages.",
    preview: "Report: Netanyahu's allies open to unity government without Ben Gvir’s party Associates of Benjamin Netanyahu have told Yashar party leader Gadi Eisenkot’s team they would accept a unity government without National Security Minister Itamar Ben Gvir's party, according to the daily Israel Hayom. Netanyahu’s associates said that Likud could let go of Otzma Yehudit (Jewish Power) if negotiations opened on a broad coalition. Speaking to figures in Eisenkot’s bloc, they also indicated US demands for Ben Gvir's Otzma Yehudit's exclusion.",
