    title: "Estonia to close Russia border after ‘sabotage’ bid",
    summary: "The move marked a sharp escalation in tensions between Estonia and Russia, part of broader hostilities linked to Moscow's war against Ukraine.",
    preview: "Tallinn, Estonia – Estonia said Sunday it would close its border with Russia after stopping what it said was an attempted arson attack by Russia’s GRU military intelligence on a drone factory. The move marked a sharp escalation in tensions between Estonia and Russia, which Tallinn sees as part of a broader campaign of hostile activity linked to Moscow’s war against Ukraine. “Estonia will close all Estonian-Russian border crossing points as of (Dec.",
    body: "Tallinn, Estonia – Estonia said Sunday it would close its border with Russia after stopping what it said was an attempted arson attack by Russia’s GRU military intelligence on a drone factory.\n\nThe move marked a sharp escalation in tensions between Estonia and Russia, which Tallinn sees as part of a broader campaign of hostile activity linked to Moscow’s war against Ukraine.\n\n“Estonia will close all Estonian-Russian border crossing points as of (Dec. 1),” Foreign Minister Margus Tsahkna posted on X, citing “clear evidence” that the GRU had ordered the attack.\n\nMoscow said it would verify whether Estonia was indeed planning to shut all crossings. “We will verify all this to see if it’s true,” Russian foreign ministry spokeswoman Maria Zakharova told TASS news agency.\n\n“But if these are (Estonia’s) real plans, then it will be seen as yet another bout of aggressive and unbridled Russophobia,” she added.\n\nEarlier Sunday, Prime Minister Kristen Michal wrote on X that the GRU had ordered a “sabotage attempt” at the Estonian defense company Threod Systems on Saturday night.\n\n“Extensive damage was averted thanks to heightened security measures and a swift reaction by law enforcement. The attackers have been detained,” he added.\n\nThe foiled attack happened in Viimsi, north of the capital, Tallinn.\n\nTsahkna, in his later post, said: “Russia must understand that hostile actions against Estonia come with consequences. Attempts to intimidate, destabilize, or undermine our security will not go unanswered.”\n\nHe also said he had informed his Finnish, Latvian and Lithuanian counterparts of the decision.\n\nSecurity forces arrested eight individuals who live in Latvia, chief prosecutor Astrid Asi told journalists.\n\nMichal called the incident “part of Russia’s broader hybrid war against Europe, with the aim of decreasing support to Ukraine and pressure on Russia.”\n\n“We will not be intimidated,” he added.\n\nThreod Systems manufactures reconnaissance and attack drones.\n\nIn August, the defense subcontractor Milrem, based in Tallinn, was targeted in an attempted arson attack and Latvian nationals were arrested.\n\nEstonia, a member of the European Union and NATO, currently has three crossing points with Russia at Narva, Luhamaa and Koidula, that allow the movement of people and goods between the two countries.\n\nRussia suspended vehicle traffic through Narva in February 2024, although pedestrians were still allowed to pass.\n\nThe crossings are among the few remaining overland links between Russia and the European Union still operating since Moscow’s full-scale invasion of Ukraine in 2022.",
